            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0290" n="216" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/622</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Francis</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-01T21:00:00+03:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 1, 1917, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 6, 2 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1941. Bolshevik demonstration for November 2 abandoned but Trotsky and associates
                    still advocating deposing of Kerensky ministry and claim demonstration be made
                    if necessary therefor. Milyukov <pb facs="0291" n="217" xml:id="pg217"/>
                    delivered strong address in Council of Republic yesterday mainly directed at the
                    Bolsheviki whom he attacked fearlessly charging deplorable conditions including
                    overwhelming Italian defeat to Bolshevik teachings. Criticized mercilessly
                    Skobelev instructions for Paris conference. I was one Ambassador present and
                    received ovation from the council excepting Bolsheviki when Milyukov
                    complimented America. Rumanian Minister and myself acknowledged [ovation],
                    Bolsheviki abstaining, at the close when the speaker paid tribute to Allies.</p>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs went to Stavka yesterday, returns tomorrow;
                    departure for Paris changed from November 3 but not definitely fixed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
